Job Summary
 We are looking for a discovery-driven Business Analyst to support digital initiatives within aviation domain. This role involves driving the end-to-end requirements journey, from shaping ambiguous business problems into clear, structured solutions—requiring strong critical thinking, storytelling, and stakeholder communication skills to drive alignment across business and technical teams.

 Mandatory Skill-set
 Bachelor’s Degree in IT, Computer Science, Engineering, or related field;
 Must have 2–5 years of experience as a Business Analyst or similar role;
 Must have strong experience in requirements gathering, analysis, and documentation (BRD, user stories, use cases);
 At least 1 year of experience in SIT/UAT and defect management;
 Hands-on experience with Agile (Scrum/Kanban) and tools such as JIRA or Confluence;
 Strong analytical thinking with the ability to structure ambiguous problems into clear solutions;
 Excellent communication and storytelling skills to engage and influence stakeholders.

 Desired Skill-set
 Experience with Design Thinking and user-centric solutioning;
 Familiarity with UX/UI collaboration tools (e.g., Figma, Miro);
 Exposure to performance or non-functional requirement testing;
 Relevant BA certifications (CBAP, PMI-PBA, IIBA-AAC) are a plus;
 Experience in aviation or enterprise platforms is advantageous.

 Responsibilities
 Gather, analyse, and translate business needs into clear functional and technical requirements;
 Structure vague problem statements into defined scope, solution approaches, and roadmaps;
 Develop BRDs, user stories, acceptance criteria, and process flows;
 Facilitate workshops and discussions to align stakeholders and drive decision-making;
 Apply Design Thinking to drive user-centric solutioning and validation;
 Collaborate with UX, developers, and architects to ensure solution feasibility and alignment;
 Define and support SIT/UAT, ensuring solutions meet business and user expectations;
 Act as the key bridge between business and tech teams, managing priorities and expectations;
 Participate in Agile ceremonies and support backlog refinement and delivery.

